DTEND:20261207T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Amsterdam Light Festival Edition 16 Open Call (
 light art\, EUR 4\,000 artist fee plus production costs)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 07 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nAmsterdam Light Festival in
 vites light art concepts for its 16th edition (2027-2028)\, presented alon
 g and on the canals of Amsterdam. WHO: creatives from all over the world\,
  individually or as a team\; multiple submissions are allowed and existing
  work may be considered.\n\nOrganisation: Amsterdam Light Festival\nLocati
 on: Amsterdam\, the Netherlands. Main call open to creatives worldwide\; t
 he Open Call X Amarte strand is for Netherlands-based makers new to light 
 art. Works are shown on the Amsterdam canals.\nAward: EUR 4\,000 artist fe
 e per selected maker\, with the costs of making the artwork and travel cov
 ered by the festival. Open Call X Amarte: EUR 4\,000 artist fee plus a EUR
  20\,000 production budget. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: Festi
 val runs 25 November 2027 to 16 January 2028 (about 7 weeks).\n\nMore: htt
 ps://amsterdamlightfestival.com/en/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://amsterdamlightfestival.com/en/open-call?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, the Netherlands. Main call open to creatives worldwide
 \; the Open Call X Amarte strand is for Netherlands-based makers new to li
 ght art. Works are shown on the Amsterdam canals.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:extra-residence-livre-objet-fabrique-pola-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160830Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:Deadline: EXTRA Residency 2027: Book-Object on Architecture\, Publi
 shing and Pedagogy (EUR 6\,000 bursary\, Fabrique POLA\, Bordeaux)
DESCRIPTION:EXTRA\, a Bordeaux association that publishes book-objects abou
 t space\, invites proposals for a residency to create a book-object at the
  crossroads of architecture\, publishing and pedagogy\, hosted at Fabrique
  POLA in Bordeaux.\n\nOrganisation: EXTRA (Editeur d'espaces)\, hosted at 
 Fabrique POLA\nLocation: Fabrique POLA\, Bordeaux\, France. No geographic 
 restriction stated\; the call is published in French.\nAward: EUR 6\,000 b
 ursary (paid in three instalments\; not multiplied for duos or collectives
 )\, up to EUR 500 for materials and up to EUR 1\,000 for travel on receipt
